<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gurung</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tamu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gurung, who call themselves Tamu, are a people of the hills of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, especially around the Annapurna range in Lamjung, Kaski and Gorkha. Speaking a Tibeto-Burman language and following Buddhist, shamanic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> practices, they served as soldiers in the armies of the Gorkha kingdom and later, in large numbers, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurkhas">Gurkhas</a> in the British and Indian armies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gurung.jpg" alt="Gurung" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SPakhrin · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gurung_Tamu_Lhosar_2018_05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
